Futya OS - Project Governance Model
===============================================================================
This document defines the decision-making framework and operational leadership
structure for the Futya OS project.

1. LEADERSHIP MODEL (BDFL)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Futya OS project operates under the Benevolent Dictator for Life (BDFL)
governance model, mirroring the historical structure of the Linux kernel.

- Project BDFL: Joao Guilherme da Silva Freitas Lima <joaoanandalima@gmail.com>

The BDFL holds absolute authority and final decision-making power over all
aspects of the project, including but not limited to:
- Kernel architecture definition and low-level specifications.
- Acceptance or rejection of code patches, subsystems, and pull requests.
- Licensing enforcement, repository access, and release schedules.

2. SUB-SYSTEM MAINTAINERS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The BDFL may designate specific Maintainers to oversee isolated components of
the system (e.g., MMU, Scheduler, Java VM Runtime, JavaScript API Bridge).
- Maintainers review incoming technical submissions for code cleanliness,
  performance bounds, and test-suite compliance.
- All decisions made by sub-system maintainers are subject to final veto or
  override by the BDFL.

3. TECHNICAL DISPUTE RESOLUTION
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
In the event of conflicts regarding design choices, resource handling, or API
implementations, the resolution path is strictly linear:
1. Technical debate driven by benchmark data and QEMU telemetry results.
2. Maintainer review within the affected sub-system.
3. Final arbitration and definitive ruling by the BDFL.
